<title>FRANCE: 1997 FRENCH BUDGET - Revenue forecasts.</title>
<headline>1997 FRENCH BUDGET - Revenue forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government gave the following revenue forecasts in its 1997 budget bill (in billions of francs unless stated).</p>
<p>				  1996	  1996	1997</p>
<p>						 revised</p>
<p> Income tax		   310.13     312.30    291.86</p>
<p> Company tax		  155.60     171.00    170.78</p>
<p> Other direct taxes	 128.04     120.57    126.06</p>
<p> Stamp duty, registrations 81.75	84.50     87.55</p>
<p> Customs duties	     158.99     159.39    162.75</p>
<p> Value added tax	    761.63     730.60    757.52</p>
<p> Other indirect taxes	46.08	45.20     46.58</p>
<p> GROSS TAX RECEIPTS     1,642.21   1,623.56  1,643.10</p>
<p> Tax reimbursements	-241.11    -245.50   -249.36</p>
<p> Other tax deductions    -252.50    -244.97   -252.16</p>
<p> NET TAX RECEIPTS	 1,148.60   1,133.08  1,141.59</p>
<p> Non-tax receipts	   115.56     127.79    127.65</p>
<p> Other receipts		16.88	19.32     17.98</p>
<p>TOTAL NET RECEIPTS</p>
<p>  Excl other receipts   1,264.16   1,260.87  1,269.24</p>
<p>  Incl other receipts   1,281.04   1,280.19  1,287.22.</p>
<p>NOTE: The government said in a note that the figures did not take account of the transfer of funds from France Telecom in exchange for the assumption of pension liabilities.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
